course: dictionary
lesson: 9092
title: Slump: sinking down or falling away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «Posture is the way you hold your body; slumping squashes the chest and belly, so there is less air and less control of the breath.» Here slumping means sitting or leaning down heavily, with the body folded in. The clues are posture, chest and breath.
explain: Now read «A big chocolate bar before a match can give a quick lift then a slump.» Quick lift and then show that energy goes up fast and then drops. So a slump here is a sudden fall in energy.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Then a sudden fall in energy» makes sense, so your meaning fits. Good readers test a meaning until the whole sentence works.
fact: Slump can be a verb (he slumped in his chair) or a noun (a sales slump).
fact: «Slumped» shows that a person is tired, upset, ill or fainting, so a slumped person may need help.
fact: A slump can also mean a sudden fall in numbers, prices or sales.
fact: In sport, a team in a slump keeps losing for a time.
fact: If someone slumps and will not wake, call an adult or the emergency number.
exercise: «Posture is the way you hold your body; slumping squashes the chest and belly.» What does slumping mean here? | *Sitting or leaning down with the body folded in | Singing loudly in a choir | Standing very tall and straight | Running fast around the field
exercise: «A big chocolate bar before a match can give a quick lift then a slump.» What does slump mean in this sentence? | A prize for winning | A long, happy sleep | *A sudden drop in energy | A bar of chocolate
exercise: Sales fell sharply, and the shop was in a slump. What is a slump? | *A time when business does badly | A new shop opening | A large box of goods | A time when the shop is very busy
test: Read «He slumped into a chair, exhausted.» What does slumped show about him? | Cold and wet | *Tired and worn out | Happy and ready to dance | Hungry for lunch
test: The team lost every match for six weeks. What does "in a slump" mean? | Playing in the rain | Winning every match | *Doing badly for a time | Training late at night
exam: Which meaning fits slump in «Prices took a slump, and many shops lost customers.»? | Stayed exactly the same | *Fell suddenly by a large amount | Rose slowly over the year | Were painted bright colours
